  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the LED. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "680385ea-c3db-5f3f-959e-99e4f4208bcb"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 41.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cd1ccd9e-9d8c-5ee0-b710-caffb494914e"))
  (text "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected, so no series diode is needed on the cell (see docs/standard.md section 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d93e193b-f690-5606-b3ce-347f497ff5c8"))
  (text "D1 = the light in the gripper's round palm, where the maker's 5 mm LED had its legs. Red through-board LED, about 1 mA through 1.3 k." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e0168fd5-48a3-58f6-82ff-0f53804d83a4"))
  (text "The maker's solder jumper (LED fed from SAO pin 1 or from GPIO2, so a badge could blink it) is not carried over: see the README." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 128.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7dfd3998-38a9-54c6-b90e-0917a6a74801"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
